<title>LUXEMBOURG: EU clears aid to German, Greek, Spanish shipyards.</title>
<headline>EU clears aid to German, Greek, Spanish shipyards.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union industry ministers gave the green light on Thursday to state aid to ailing shipyards in Germany, Greece and Spain, an EU source said.</p>
<p>The ministers reached a so-called political agreement on a proposal from the European Commission to grant the request from the countries concerned to help the restructuring efforts of the yards.  </p>
<p>No details were immediately available.</p>
<p>The European Commission's proposal, which has sparked U.S. criticism, needed the backing of a qualified majority of EU member states.</p>
<p>The EU's Nordic member states and Britain had voiced opposition to the plan but they were not by themselves be able to block approval.</p>
<p>In return for approval of the aid, Germany, Spain and Greece said previously they would not pay any more rescue or restructuring aid to the shipyards.</p>
</text>
